# Script:  greedy_orbits.rlab
# System:  Greedy decoding of the trained Lesson 18 bigram viewed as an
#          autonomous map on its 3-element state space {a, b, c}; the KV
#          cache viewed as the state of the generation loop.
# Concept: A Markov-k model under greedy decoding is a deterministic map on
#          |V|^k states, so every orbit is eventually periodic with transient
#          + period <= |V|^k.  For the bigram (3 states) "abab..." is the only
#          long-run behaviour from every start.  The generation loop is a
#          closed loop with unit delay whose state -- the KV cache -- grows
#          as 2 t d_head numbers per head per layer.
# Equations:
#   x_{t+1} = argmax_i P(i | x_t)                        (autonomous map)
#   x_{t+1} = g(f_theta(x_{1:t}), eps_t)                 (closed loop, unit delay)
#   KV state at step t = 2 * t * d_head per head per layer
# Units:   tokens are 1-based ids; state sizes in numbers (fp16 = 2 bytes).

run "../../lib/bigram_lm.rlab"

# === 1. Train the model ===
seed(18);
pat = [1, 2, 3, 2];
corpus = zeros(60);
for i = 1:60
  corpus(i) = pat(mod(i - 1, 4) + 1);
end
[E, W] = train_bigram_lm(corpus(1:50), 3, 4, 600, 0.15, 0.015, 60);

names = {"a", "b", "c"};
function s = seq_to_str(seq, names)
  s = "";
  for i = 1:length(seq)
    s = s + names(seq(i));
  end
end

# === 2. The argmax map and its orbits from every start ===
function nxt = argmax_step(x, E, W)
  nxt = argmax(softmax(E(x, :) * W));
end
for s = 1:3
  print("argmax map:", names(s), "->", names(argmax_step(s, E, W)));
end
for s = 1:3
  orbit = zeros(9);  orbit(1) = s;
  for t = 1:8
    orbit(t + 1) = argmax_step(orbit(t), E, W);
  end
  j = 8;                                   # previous visit of the final state
  while j >= 1 && orbit(j) != orbit(9)
    j = j - 1;
  end
  print("orbit from", names(s), ":", seq_to_str(orbit, names), "  period", 9 - j);
end
print("bound: transient + period <= |V|^k = 3 states");

# === 3. The KV cache as the loop's state: dimension grows with t ===
d_head = 4;
for t = [1, 2, 4, 8]
  print("toy head (d_head = 4): KV state at t =", t, "->", 2 * t * d_head, "numbers");
end
L_layers = 32;  H_heads = 32;  d_head_prod = 128;
for T_ctx = [1024, 8192]
  n_cache = 2 * L_layers * H_heads * T_ctx * d_head_prod;
  print("production (32 x 32 heads, d_head 128) at T =", T_ctx, ":", n_cache, "numbers =", n_cache * 2 / 1e9, "GB fp16");
end
